B.WL=new A.dW("A complete idle simulation prototype developed in Unity using modular gameplay architecture, reusable systems, event-driven programming, Addressables, object pooling, and scalable gameplay design. The project focuses on clean architecture and maintainable code rather than game-specific implementation.",null,B.dA,null,null,null,null)
B.WM=new A.dW("A modular Unity framework focused on endless world streaming, reusable gameplay architecture, ScriptableObject-driven systems, extensible AI, and scalable world management. Built to rapidly create endless driving, survival, combat, and exploration games by reusing the same core systems.",null,B.dA,null,null,null,null)
B.WN=new A.dW("A complete offline Ludo game featuring multiple gameplay modes, including Classic, Quick Match, and Killer Mode, each introducing unique rule variations while sharing a common gameplay framework. The game supports 2, 3, and 4 player matches against AI opponents or local multiplayer with friends on a single device, including team-based gameplay. A modular turn-based architecture manages token movement, dice logic, captures, safe zones, home progression, and victory conditions. AI opponents feature distinct personalities, ranging from aggressive strategies that prioritize eliminating opponents to defensive strategies focused on completing the race efficiently. The project also includes Google and Facebook authentication for player profiles, persistent progression, polished UI, animations, and optimized mobile performance. The source code is not available because the project belongs to my previous employer, but the published game is available below.",null,B.dA,null,null,null,null)
B.WP=new A.dW("Download Resume",null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.WR=new A.dW("A published tattoo simulation game where players create tattoos by selecting ink colors, switching tattoo machines, and progressively completing detailed artwork through texture-based painting. The project features reusable pixel-level coloring technology, multi-stage tattoo progression, ScriptableObject-based architecture, event-driven gameplay systems, persistent progression, economy, daily rewards, daily tasks, spin wheel, unlockable cosmetics, and production-ready UI designed for scalable mobile game development. The source code is not available because the project belongs to my previous employer, but the published Google Play version is available below.",null,B.dA,null,null,null,null)
B.WS=new A.dW("A modular casual game framework developed in Unity featuring a data-driven water sort engine, texture-based coloring system, custom shaders, reusable UI architecture, Addressables-based content streaming, ScriptableObject runtime database, event-driven communication, and scalable gameplay systems including daily rewards, tasks, progression, and weighted reward mechanics. Designed for rapid reskinning and reuse across multiple puzzle and casual game projects.",null,B.dA,null,null,null,null)
B.lp=new A.dW("View GitHub Repository",null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.WT=new A.dW("A published 3D traffic puzzle game where players guide colored passengers through a grid-based environment to board matching ships. The gameplay is built around a tile-based movement system with directional movement rules, occupancy validation, pathfinding, passenger queuing, and fail-state detection when waiting areas become blocked. Levels are created from reusable ScriptableObject data that defines passenger placement, ship configurations, and puzzle layouts, allowing large amounts of content to be produced without scene duplication. The project also includes power-ups such as Undo and direct passenger transport, progression systems, production-ready UI, optimized mobile gameplay, and a modular architecture designed for scalable level creation. The source code is not available because the project belongs to my previous employer, but the published Google Play version is available below.",null,B.dA,null,null,null,null)
